---
import { loadKvm } from '../../lib/kvm';
import { benchmarkContext } from '../../data/project';

// Read from bench/results/kvm/table/ at build time: every cell is a number the
// scripts of the repository derived, never typed here.
const rows = loadKvm();
const kvmContext = 'KVM, one bare metal host: AMD Ryzen 5 PRO 3600, one virtual processor';
---

<section class="kvm-section" aria-labelledby="kvm-title">
  <div class="wrapper">
    <header class="section-header">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Hardware acceleration</p>
      <h2 id="kvm-title" class="text-title">The same rig under KVM</h2>
      <p class="text-lead">
        The ratios of the emulator do not all hold. On one bare metal host some are smaller, three
        reversed, and two defects of the kernel were found and fixed along the way.
      </p>
    </header>

    <p class="scroll-hint" aria-hidden="true">Scroll sideways: the KVM columns and the direction are to the right.</p>

    <div class="table-card">
      <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Emulation and KVM table">
        <table>
          <caption class="sr-only">
            Rabbit against Linux 7.3.0 with mitigations off, under emulation and under KVM, with the ratio
            of each and whether the direction held.
          </caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col" rowspan="2">Metric</th>
              <th scope="colgroup" colspan="3" class="group">{benchmarkContext}</th>
              <th scope="colgroup" colspan="3" class="group">KVM</th>
              <th scope="col" rowspan="2">Direction</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Rabbit</th>
              <th scope="col">Linux</th>
              <th scope="col">Ratio</th>
              <th scope="col">Rabbit</th>
              <th scope="col">Linux</th>
              <th scope="col">Ratio</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              rows.map((row) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">
                    {row.metric}
                  </th>
                  <td class="value">{row.rabbitTcg}</td>
                  <td class="value">{row.referenceTcg}</td>
                  <td class="value">{row.ratioTcg}</td>
                  <td class="value strong">{row.rabbitKvm}</td>
                  <td class="value">{row.referenceKvm}</td>
                  <td class="value strong">{row.ratioKvm}</td>
                  <td class={`reading${row.reading === 'reverses' ? ' reversed' : ''}`}>{row.reading}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ul class="notes">
      <li>
        A ratio above 1 means Rabbit is better, whichever the unit. The reference is Linux 7.3.0 with
        mitigations off. A tie is a difference smaller than twice the spread between the runs.
      </li>
      <li>
        The left figures ran under {benchmarkContext}, one run each. The right figures ran under {kvmContext},
        five runs, the median of the medians. Only the right ones can support a statement about wall clock
        time, and only on that host.
      </li>
      <li>
        The raw data, the five versions of the kernel measured on the way, and the diagnostics are in{' '}
        <code>bench/results/kvm/</code>.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .kvm-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .section-header {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .section-eyebrow {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--font-medium);
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .section-eyebrow {
      color: var(--accent-on-dark);
    }
  }

  .section-header h2 {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .table-card {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .table-wrap:focus-visible {
    outline-offset: -2px;
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 980px;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  thead th {
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    text-align: left;
    font-weight: var(--font-medium);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  thead th.group {
    text-align: center;
    border-inline: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  tbody th,
  tbody td {
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  tbody tr:last-child th,
  tbody tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  tbody th {
    font-weight: var(--font-medium);
    color: var(--text);
    text-align: left;
    min-width: 12rem;
    position: sticky;
    inset-inline-start: 0;
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
  }

  thead th[rowspan] {
    position: sticky;
    inset-inline-start: 0;
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    min-width: 12rem;
  }

  .scroll-hint {
    display: none;
    margin-block-end: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .scroll-hint {
      display: block;
    }

    .table-wrap {
      background:
        linear-gradient(to right, var(--bg-elevated), var(--bg-elevated)) left top,
        linear-gradient(to right, var(--bg-elevated), var(--bg-elevated)) right top,
        linear-gradient(to right, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12), transparent) left top,
        linear-gradient(to left, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12), transparent) right top;
      background-size: 1.5rem 100%, 1.5rem 100%, 0.75rem 100%, 0.75rem 100%;
      background-attachment: local, local, scroll, scroll;
      background-repeat: no-repeat;
    }
  }

  .value {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    white-space: nowrap;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .value.strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: var(--font-medium);
  }

  .reading {
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .reading.reversed {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: var(--font-semibold);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  .notes {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-md);
    padding-inline-start: 1.1em;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }
</style>
